# Autonomous reduction of USC Mech II — final report

## 1. Task and chosen application domain

Parent mechanism: USC Mech II (111 species, 784 reactions; `mech/parent.yaml`,
converted from `USC_Mech_II.cti` by cti2yaml/Cantera 3.1). High-temperature
C0–C4 hydrocarbon combustion chemistry.

Chosen application domain (declared a priori, matched to the mechanism's native
scope and to the coverage of obtainable experimental data):

- Fuels: H2, CO, CH4, CH3OH, C2H6, C2H4, C2H2, C3H8, C3H6, n-C4H10, i-C4H10
  (the FFCM-2/SFCPD "foundational fuels" set; CO covered only by blends and one
  CO-oxidation IDT series — see limitations).
- Observables: shock-tube ignition delay time (IDT) and laminar flame speed (Su).
  These are the two experimentally measurable macroscopic observables required
  by the task; species-by-species agreement is NOT required.
- Conditions: IDT T ≈ 1050–2230 K, P ≈ 0.3–260 atm, phi ≈ 0.1–5, Ar/N2 bath;
  Su Tu ≈ 295–470 K, P ≈ 0.5–60 atm, phi ≈ 0.03–4, air/O2-N2 oxidizer.
- Omitted: RCM/low-T (T<1000 K) chemistry, NOx/soot/PAH observables, flame
  structure (speciation), real-gas/high-pressure nonideal effects, blends other
  than H2+CO. Consequences: the reduced mechanisms are NOT validated for
  low-temperature heat release, ignition with NTC behavior, or emissions.

## 2. Experimental evidence base

(data/exp/MANIFEST.md; raw downloads in data/exp/raw/)

- Primary source: FFCM-2 validation targets (Stanford, SFCPD-derived), the only
  public machine-readable SFCPD content (1192 target records retrieved from the
  FFCM-2 website source repository). IDT: 449 points/240 series over 10 fuels,
  with per-study diagnostics and multiplicative uncertainties. Su: 272 points/
  110 target groups over 11 fuels with +/- cm/s uncertainties and method labels.
  52 records dropped by us (40 He-bath cases — He is not an element in USC-II;
  12 with composition-sum typos flagged in the manifest). Source-data defects
  (19 phi/composition mismatches, 1 mislabeled series) kept verbatim, flagged,
  and handled by using compositions rather than phi fields.
- ReSpecTh: anonymous metadata catalogued (2891 relevant datasets), data files
  login-blocked (HTTP 401); no accounts created per task rules. Coverage that
  exists but is unreachable is documented (e.g. 227 H2 IDT series).
- CloudFlame unreachable; ChemKED ruled out (large fuels only); SFCPD pandas
  database itself has no public download.
- Multi-study Su values are FFCM-2 evaluated averages (labeled as such), not
  single measurements; repeated points within a series are treated as one
  dataset, not independent studies.

## 3. Method

### 3.1 Simulation workflow (built for this run)

- Cantera 3.0.1, pinned identically on the local driver and the remote 64-core
  compute node (offline wheels; verified bit-identical Su on a test case).
- IDT: 0-D constant-volume adiabatic reactor; IDT = time of max dT/dt.
  Diagnostic proxy note: experiments use OH*/CH*/pressure criteria; max-dT/dt is
  a proxy (secondary max-d[OH]/dt diagnostic computed for comparison).
- Su: 1-D freely-propagating premixed flame, mixture-averaged transport (as
  specified by the mechanism), adaptive grid refinement; wider-domain retry on
  non-convergence.
- Batch runners with multiprocessing; incremental result writes (crash-safe).

### 3.2 Reduction strategy

Two-stage skeletal reduction, error-controlled against the parent on a
development matrix (264 cases: 198 dilute-ignition + 66 premixed-flame points
spanning all 11 fuels, phi 0.5–2, T 1100–1800 K, P 1–10 atm), then confirmed
against the independent experimental set (669 cases).

1. Species selection: directed relation graph (DRG) interaction coefficients
   r_AB sampled along autoignition trajectories (0-D constant-volume, up to
   ignition; flames excluded from sampling because preheat/post-flame states
   inject spurious r_AB~1 edges, verified). Seeds = 11 fuels + O2; AR/N2 always
   retained. Aggregation over states is the MEAN, not the DRGEP-max: with ~2000
   states across 11 fuels, max-aggregation saturates ~100/111 species at r_AB=1
   and destroys discrimination (demonstrated; mean-aggregation restores a
   chemically sensible ranking). Species ladder (40/50/60/70/80) by maximin
   bottleneck distance.
2. Reaction trimming: per-reaction DRG importance J_i (mean-aggregated);
   lowest-importance reactions removed in batches, each batch verified on the
   development matrix.
3. Every candidate verified to load in Cantera, conserve all elements
   (reaction-level atom balance), and run the full development matrix.
   No rate or thermo-chemistry parameters are ever modified: reduction is
   purely deletion of whole species/reactions.

Development-matrix acceptance: max IDT log-ratio <= 0.30 (2x), mean <= 0.05;
max Su relative error <= 10%, mean <= 3% vs parent.

### 3.3 Tool verification

- DRGEP pipeline cross-checked on GRI-Mech 3.0 (built into Cantera): reduced
  53 sp/325 rxn -> 34 sp/205 rxn for CH4 targets; IDT error 1.00x (6 cases),
  Su error <= 0.35% (3 cases, Su never sampled — genuine extrapolation);
  element balance passed. Implementation pitfalls found and fixed during
  verification are documented in the notebook.
- Flame solver spot-checked against literature-consistent values
  (Su(CH4/air, 300 K, 1 atm) = 36.3 cm/s).

## 4. Results

### 4.1 Parent mechanism vs experiments (reference)

Reference for "useful accuracy": the parent's own error envelope against the
669 experimental targets (results/parent_exp.csv; per-point sim vs exp with
diagnostics kept). All 669 cases completed (604 ignited/solved, 65 predicted
no thermal ignition within 5x the experimental delay — concentrated in very
lean/dilute shock-tube mixtures and the lowest-T points; constant-volume
homogeneous idealization is weakest there, and facility pressure-rise is not
modeled).

- IDT (n=384 ignited): MAE 0.209 dex, RMSE 0.276 dex, max 1.12 dex,
  76% of points within a factor 2 of experiment. Known parent weak spots kept
  as reference (not reduction failures): CH3OH MAE 0.457 dex, C2H6 0.309 dex.
- Su (n=220): MAE 4.45 cm/s, mean relative error 10.5%, max 39.4 cm/s,
  87% of points within 20% of experiment (per-fuel: C2H2 5.8% to CH3OH 17.4%).
- The two IDT diagnostics (max dT/dt vs max d[OH]/dt) agree with median ratio
  1.00 (mean 0.06 dex); max-dT/dt agrees slightly better with the experimental
  onset diagnostics (MAE 0.209 vs 0.268 dex) and is used throughout.

A reduced mechanism is accepted only if its experimental metrics stay within
this parent envelope: IDT MAE increase <= 0.03 dex and within-2x fraction
drop <= 3 points, Su MAE increase <= 1 cm/s, and no systematic new failure
mode (element imbalance, solver non-convergence, new no-ignition regions).

### 4.2 Accuracy/complexity trade-off (development matrix)

Development matrix: 264 cases (198 dilute-ignition + 66 premixed-flame points,
11 fuels, phi 0.5-2, IDT T 1100-1800 K P 1.5-10 atm; flames Tu 300 K P 1-5
atm), errors measured against the parent (fidelity, not experimental accuracy).
Ladder from the mean-aggregated DRG ranking (H2O2 force-kept):

| mech | species | reactions | IDT mean dex | IDT max dex | Su mean % | Su max % |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| cand_40 | 40 | 260 | 0.191 | 1.27 | 11.7 | 92.8 |
| cand_50 | 50 | 365 | 0.102 | 1.27 | 5.2 | 29.8 |
| cand_60 | 60 | 483 | 0.064 | 1.30 | 4.2 | 25.3 |
| cand_65 | 65 | 528 | 0.023 | 0.61 | 0.95 | 4.6 |
| cand_70 | 70 | 563 | 0.009 | 0.16 | 1.1 | 3.9 |
