Reaction space trims ~10% for free; beyond that the Su tolerance (10%) breaks.

### 4.3 Final candidates vs experiments

All 669 experimental targets per mechanism; "fidelity" = reduced vs parent on
those same targets (generalization: none of these conditions was used for
reduction or candidate selection).

| mech | sp/rxn | IDT MAE dex (parent 0.209) | IDT within 2x (76%) | Su MAE cm/s (4.45) | Su within 20% (87%) | fidelity IDT mean/max dex | fidelity Su mean/max % | ok/noign/fail |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| sk80 | 80/614 | 0.210 | 76% | 4.31 | 88% | 0.006 / 0.099 | 0.6 / 3.4 | 605/64/0 |
| sk70 | 70/563 | 0.209 | 76% | 4.36 | 87% | 0.009 / 0.179 | 1.4 / 11.0 | 603/66/0 |
| sk70_t0.10 | 70/507 | 0.212 | 75% | 4.60 | 86% | 0.010 / 0.179 | 1.9 / 17.0 | 604/65/0 |

All three candidates stay inside the parent's experimental error envelope
(acceptance: IDT MAE +<=0.03 dex, within-2x -<=3 points, Su MAE +<=1 cm/s):
- sk80: IDT MAE delta +0.001 dex, within-2x delta 0, Su MAE delta -0.14 cm/s;
  fidelity to parent 0.006 dex mean / 0.099 max. Conservative choice.
- sk70: IDT MAE delta +0.000 dex, within-2x delta 0 points, Su MAE delta -0.09
  cm/s. Only per-fuel change is C2H2 IDT (MAE 0.307 -> 0.326 dex), the known
  low-T C2-chain residual. Primary choice.
- sk70_t0.10: IDT MAE delta +0.003 dex, within-2x delta -1 point, Su MAE
  delta +0.15 cm/s. Trimming 56 reactions is experimentally free.
- Zero solver failures in all reduced-mechanism runs; no-ignition predictions
  match the parent's on 64-65/65 cases (disagreements: 0-1). Differences go
  both ways: sk80 even ignites one very-rich CH4 case (ign_CH4_20, phi=5,
  1687 K) that the parent does not, landing closer to the experimental value.
- Audit of the 56 reactions dropped in sk70_t0.10: dominated by radical-
  radical and minor-channel reactions (C3/C4 radical disproportionation,
  duplicate recombination channels); a few fast channels (C2H5+H, CH3O+H)
  whose pathways are redundant — removal empirically invisible on all targets.

