## 5. Discussion: trade-offs, failures, limitations

### 5.1 What the trade-off looks like

Compression achieved: 111 sp/784 rxn -> **70 sp/563 rxn (sk70)** and
**70 sp/507 rxn (sk70_t0.10)**, i.e. -37% species and -28%/-35% reactions, with
experimental behavior indistinguishable from the parent across 669 targets
(11 fuels). On the development matrix the fidelity ladder (Table in 4.2) shows
a sharp knee at ~70 species: errors grow gently 111->70, then explode (max Su
error 25-93% at 40-60 species; max IDT ratio up to 20x). The knee is set by the
C2 oxygenate chain (HCCO/CH2CO/CH3CO...) for low-T acetylene ignition and by
C3/C4 fragmentation completeness; the 60->70 step repairs it. Reaction trimming
beyond ~10% breaks the flame-speed tolerance first (Su is more sensitive to
reaction removal than IDT here).

Context (literature, agents/<id>/lit_context.md): published USC-II reductions
reach 13-33 species but are all application-specific (single fuel / narrow
domain, some with retuned rates); no general-purpose reduced USC-II exists.
FFCM-2 covers the same C0-C4 domain at 96 sp/1054 rxn. Our 70-species pair
therefore fills a real gap: domain-wide (11 fuels, IDT + Su), parameter-free
(pure deletion), experimentally validated against the parent's own envelope.

### 5.2 Where accuracy is lost (honest accounting)

- C2H2 low-T ignition is the only systematic residual: dev max 0.16 dex at
  1100 K; on experiments, C2H2 IDT MAE 0.307 (parent) -> 0.326 (sk70) dex and
  one case where the parent ignites late (13x over experiment) and sk70 does
  not ignite within 5x. This is the price of the 60->70 boundary.
- The parent's own weak spots are inherited, not caused, by reduction:
  CH3OH IDT MAE 0.457 dex and C2H6 0.309 dex (USC-II limitations, visible in
  the identical parent numbers).
- 65 cases (15%) predict no thermal ignition within 5x of the experimental
  delay for BOTH parent and reduced mechanisms: very lean/dilute shock-tube
  mixtures and lowest-T points, where the constant-volume homogeneous model
  (no facility pressure-rise, no boundary-layer effects) is the limiting
  assumption, not the chemistry.

### 5.3 Limitations of this run

- Coverage gaps: neat-CO experimental data unobtainable from allowed public
  sources (only H2+CO blends + one mislabeled series); H2 IDT only 2 points;
  ReSpecTh data files login-blocked (2891 datasets catalogued but locked);
  40 He-bath records dropped (He not in USC-II elements). CO and H2 ignition
  validation is therefore thinner than the C1-C4 part.
- IDT diagnostic is a proxy (max dT/dt); experimental diagnostics vary
  (OH*/CH*/pressure). Shown to agree within 0.06 dex on median, and the
  reduced-vs-parent comparison is diagnostic-independent anyway.
- SFCPD values are FFCM-2 evaluated targets (some multi-study averages), used
  as the best available public machine-readable form; original per-point
  uncertainty provenance not independently re-derived.
- Development matrix capped at T >= 1100 K; nothing is claimed for RCM /
  low-T heat-release regimes.
- Only deletion was used (no rate retuning). Retuning a handful of rates
  (as Lytras 2019 and Liu 2018 do) could compress further but was out of
  scope: it would blur the fidelity/accuracy separation this run keeps.
- Resource-limited single pass: the ladder used one ranking (mean-aggregated
  DRG); a second reduction round with error-driven elimination might find a
  few more removable species near the knee.

### 5.4 How retrieved knowledge changed the work

- ChemKED was ruled out by direct inspection (large fuels only) -> SFCPD via
  FFCM-2 validation pages became the primary source; ReSpecTh was found
  login-blocked and is reported as an availability result, not assumed data.
- FFCM-2 target records carry source-data defects (phi/composition mismatches,
  a mislabeled series, composition-sum typos) — found by the data researcher,
  handled by simulating compositions (not phi fields) and dropping 52 records.
- The literature scan confirmed no general-purpose reduced USC-II exists and
  that published small mechanisms narrow the domain; this justified keeping
  all 11 fuels in the development matrix rather than reducing per-fuel.
- Methodologically, the broad target set broke the standard DRGEP-max
  selector (saturation), which forced the mean-aggregation fix — the main
  methodological finding of the run.

